**Date:** 28 October 2026 · **Proposed by:** Rafał Łuczun with Codex

## Context

The [review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review/) shows that subjects and browser-derived
intake tags do not reliably identify a defect. An incident can contain several causes.
This proposal replaces [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) when accepted by the desk.
Record 0001 is preserved unchanged.

## Decision

Read the body and consult tenant locale, booking form version and channel. Merge only
when the cause is demonstrated to be the same. For this snapshot, `causes.ts` distinguishes
the shared month-first parser from the booking-v3 month-first hint on a day-first form.
Do not use browser locale, intake tags or subject equality as the deciding evidence.

Count each report ID once. Keep evidence that contradicts a classification visible and
request a reproduction. Missing tenants or an unexplained symptom need investigation;
leave them apart until a cause is established. Reconcile new arrivals while the desk works.

## Examples and consequences

<DedupeExplorer />

This original explorer demonstrates the exported tenant/form/channel classifier only.
Its “same cause — merge” label is preliminary; it does not read the bodies or establish
that merging is justified. Apply the evidence checks above before any merge.

This takes more reading than subject matching, but prevents a queued fix from hiding a
different defect. It also merges different subjects that describe the same cause. Review
the rule when new products, forms or symptoms appear; the current classifier covers only
the date problems evidenced in this export.

